    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "body": "# ZORR BLATT — VISUAL TABOO #1\n\nSTATUS = ACTIVE GLOBAL PRODUCTION LAW\nSCOPE = ALL CHARACTER / ENVIRONMENT / TEXTURE / FX / SALVADOR / GENERATION / ART DIRECTION\n\n## HARD LAW\n\n`NO EXTERNAL AESTHETIC BINDINGS`\n\nZORR BLATT must never be aesthetically defined by an external genre, artist, studio, franchise, existing character, named visual style, or external image-reference identity.\n\n### FORBIDDEN\n\n- prompts/instructions such as `anime style`, `manga style`, or equivalent genre labels used as style authority;\n- `like X`, `in the style of Y`, `make it look like [artist/studio/franchise/character]`;\n- using external images as ZORR style targets or aesthetic templates;\n- importing another character/image's face/body/costume/silhouette language into ZORR identity;\n- internet image search for aesthetic imitation;\n- describing ZORR production law by analogy to external IP or visual brands.\n\n### ALLOWED\n\n- internal ZORR visual anchors explicitly approved by OWNER;\n- mathematical / measurable ZORR drawing and texture laws;\n- character source images only as `SOURCE / IDENTITY EVIDENCE`, never automatic style authority;\n- internet/upstream research for code, algorithms, mathematics, rendering methods, documentation, QC methods and open-source implementation;\n- generic technical terms that describe measurable rendering behavior without binding ZORR to an external aesthetic identity.\n\n## SALVADOR LAW\n\nSALVADOR prompts, conditioning manifests, datasets and training captions must not contain external aesthetic bindings.\n\nSALVADOR learns:\n\n`ZORR INTERNAL STYLE LAW + CHARACTER TRUTH + GEOMETRY/POSE CONSTRAINTS`\n\nnot:\n\n`EXTERNAL STYLE LABEL / EXTERNAL IMAGE IMITATION`.\n\nAny external-aesthetic binding in a production task is a fail-closed error:\n\n`VISUAL_TABOO_1_VIOLATION = FAIL`\n\n## RESEARCH BOUNDARY\n\nExternal research remains encouraged for acceleration, but only for:\n\n`OPEN CODE -> MATH -> ALGORITHMS -> DOCUMENTATION -> QC`\n\nnot for aesthetic imitation.\n\n## DURABLE MEANING\n\nThis law supersedes prior casual descriptions that compared ZORR to \"anime\" or any other external visual category. Such labels are non-authoritative and must not be used going forward.\n",
